0912.4184	future_work	In the future, we will extended our logic to deal with more programming language concepts: function calls, function pointers, class/object, generics, {{formula:91c4b1a0-a02f-47a7-aa0a-f966fd587257}} .	For example, for all assignment statements of the form {{formula:bb7deb2c-702c-42a1-be73-67bf868dda8f}} , the premise that {{formula:8026ae25-98dd-4ca7-966a-5993856479b1}} can be proved by pointer analyer easily. For assignment statements of the form {{formula:368d9ee4-7276-4a7f-90e5-0f00b0c02474}} , the premise {{formula:c7862e7c-0542-4f8a-a448-3239f3340210}} of the proof rule ASSIGN-ST can also be verified automatically in many cases. In the future, we will extended our logic to deal with more programming language concepts: function calls, function pointers, class/object, generics, {{formula:91c4b1a0-a02f-47a7-aa0a-f966fd587257}} . At the mean time, we will try to build a library of pre-defined DRFs, MSFs, and their properties for frequently used data structures.	0.9
