1009.2123	future_work	A full three-dimensional treatment of the assemblies would allow inclusion of effects, such as the variation of the centroid of fission over the cycle.	Finally, as noted earlier, we used an ORIGEN simulation of the SONGS Unit 2 reactor core. Assemblies were assumed to have no spatial extent: the only spatial information in our calculation was the variation in distance of each pointlike assembly from the detector. A full three-dimensional treatment of the assemblies would allow inclusion of effects, such as the variation of the centroid of fission over the cycle.	0.85
1010.1307	limitation	However, exact modelling of all the distortion effects on all scales is difficult, and when such modelling cannot be done exactly, these effects introduces systematic errors in the measurement of the BAO ridge's scale.	Due to the distortion effects, confirming the significance of the baryon ridge detection becomes a demanding process, since each distortion effect has to be carefully modelled. However, exact modelling of all the distortion effects on all scales is difficult, and when such modelling cannot be done exactly, these effects introduces systematic errors in the measurement of the BAO ridge's scale. Despite these, the radial BAO size method still surpasses the age method in precision.	0.9
1010.1307	open_problem	Currently there is some dispute over the claimed detection of radial BAO and measurement of \(H(z)\) in \cite:c6b5602add6162749d5b9b040734bb4d67be55aa.	Currently there is some dispute over the claimed detection of radial BAO and measurement of \(H(z)\) in \cite:c6b5602add6162749d5b9b040734bb4d67be55aa. \cite:90e09cb13ef8cb59be938092366cefa5e5e009c1 argued against the methods in \cite:c6b5602add6162749d5b9b040734bb4d67be55aa and the statistical significance of the claimed BAO detection. \cite:0ad1916d7bf8832b5bf6aac122adac231ffe82d9 analyzed the SDSS DR7 sample of LRGs and obtained similar results to \cite:c6b5602add6162749d5b9b040734bb4d67be55aa, but offered another interpretation using the \(\omega\) statistic and the Bayesian evidence \cite:db51dce634a9bb966cc9ff8edb809c5bea4cbc39 that disfavors a statistically significant detection. On the other hand, the recent research of \cite:35484b9519c3903f7276e42069cbec4d077a8e58 claims that the radial BAO feature is not a fluke, albeit certain assumptions made this re-assessment somewhat optimistic. The authors of \cite:c6b5602add6162749d5b9b040734bb4d67be55aa also defended their work in \cite:3b4869a87c4cae46a590e27608c914b6250be09e. We refer to these variety of arguments and opinions to remind the reader of these ongoing investigations.	0.85
